# MSA Schedule 4 — Service Credits

> Module Service_credits

This module encodes the money half of Schedule 4: the credit base (L-2.7), the
L-4.1 band table, the L-4.2 cap, L-4.3's double override of both, and L-4.4's
forfeiture. It consumes the `availability_percentage` computed by
`Availability` as an input, so the two judgement inputs that L-2.5 lifts —
`force_majeure_event_certified` and `outage_attributable_to_customer` — sit
upstream of every figure this module produces.

L-4.4 is a HYBRID clause: the arrears test and its consequence are exact, but
they bite only on an **undisputed** invoice, and whether the Customer's
assertion of a dispute takes an invoice outside the exception is a
characterisation the Schedule does not define. It is therefore the judgement
input `invoice_undisputed`, which this module applies and never infers.

Two things to keep straight about `availability_percentage`. It is the **L-2.3
figure, already rounded to two decimal places** — every comparison below is
made against the rounded number because that is what the defined term means,
so an unrounded 99.895% arrives here as 99.90% and earns nothing. And it is a
percentage on the 0–100 scale, not a fraction: 99.90, not 0.9990.

## Prologue — declarations

```catala-metadata
declaration scope MonthlyServiceCharge:
  input charges_for_the_service content money
  input one_off_charges content money
  input professional_services_charges content money
  input pass_through_charges content money
  output monthly_service_charge content money

declaration scope ServiceCredit:
  # The L-2.3 Availability Percentage, rounded to two decimal places, on the
  # 0-100 scale.
  input availability_percentage content decimal
  input monthly_service_charge content money
  # L-4.4: days for which the Customer has been in arrears of the invoice.
  input arrears_days content integer
  # L-4.4: JUDGEMENT INPUT — whether that invoice is undisputed.
  input invoice_undisputed content boolean
  output credit_percentage content decimal
  output credit_cap_percentage content decimal
  output credit_payable_percentage content decimal
  output credit_amount content money
```

## L-2.7 Monthly Service Charge

| MSA-SCH4 L-2.7 (004-msa-sla-credits.md:55)
|
| "Monthly Service Charge" means the charges payable by the Customer in
| respect of the Service for the Measurement Period in question, excluding
| one-off charges, professional services charges and pass-through charges.

The definition is inclusive of the charges for the Service in the period and
exclusive of three named categories, so it is a subtraction and not a
selection: `charges_for_the_service` is the gross figure for the Measurement
Period and the three exclusions come off it.

```catala
scope MonthlyServiceCharge:
  definition monthly_service_charge equals
    charges_for_the_service
    - one_off_charges
    - professional_services_charges
    - pass_through_charges
```

## L-4.1 The band table

| MSA-SCH4 L-4.1 (004-msa-sla-credits.md:66)
|
| Where the Availability Percentage in a Measurement Period is less than
| 99.90%, the Customer is entitled to a Service Credit calculated as a percentage
| of the Monthly Service Charge as follows:
|
|   (a) less than 99.90% but not less than 99.50%: 5%;
|   (b) less than 99.50% but not less than 99.00%: 10%;
|   (c) less than 99.00% but not less than 98.00%: 20%;
|   (d) less than 98.00%: 30%.

L-4.1 engages only "where the Availability Percentage ... is less than
99.90%", so the base case is no credit and the four bands are exceptions to
it. Exactly 99.90% is outside L-4.1 altogether and earns nothing, because
L-3.1 is met at 99.90%.

Each band boundary is exclusive above and inclusive below — "less than 99.50%
but not less than 99.00%" — so exactly 99.50% falls in band (a) and not band
(b), exactly 99.00% in band (b), exactly 98.00% in band (c). The four
conditions are mutually exclusive, so they share one label and form a single
node of the hierarchy rather than competing.

```catala
scope ServiceCredit:
  label l4_1_base definition credit_percentage equals 0%

  label l4_1 exception l4_1_base definition credit_percentage
    under condition
      (availability_percentage < 99.90) and (availability_percentage >= 99.50)
    consequence equals 5%

  label l4_1 exception l4_1_base definition credit_percentage
    under condition
      (availability_percentage < 99.50) and (availability_percentage >= 99.00)
    consequence equals 10%

  label l4_1 exception l4_1_base definition credit_percentage
    under condition
      (availability_percentage < 99.00) and (availability_percentage >= 98.00)
    consequence equals 20%

  label l4_1 exception l4_1_base definition credit_percentage
    under condition availability_percentage < 98.00
    consequence equals 30%

  definition credit_amount equals
    monthly_service_charge * credit_payable_percentage
```

## L-4.2 The aggregate cap

| MSA-SCH4 L-4.2 (004-msa-sla-credits.md:75)
|
| The maximum aggregate Service Credit in respect of any Measurement
| Period is 30% of the Monthly Service Charge.

L-4.2 is unconditional — it applies "in respect of any Measurement Period" —
so the cap has no guard, and the cap is what it operates on
`credit_payable_percentage` to do: the lesser of the L-4.1 percentage and the
ceiling. On the L-4.1 table alone the cap never bites, since band (d) is
already 30%; it bites once L-4.3 raises the credit to 50%, which is why L-4.3
has to raise the ceiling as well.

```catala
scope ServiceCredit:
  label l4_2 definition credit_cap_percentage equals 30%

  definition credit_payable_percentage equals
    if credit_percentage > credit_cap_percentage
    then credit_cap_percentage
    else credit_percentage
```

## L-4.3 Below 95.00%

| MSA-SCH4 L-4.3 (004-msa-sla-credits.md:78)
|
| By way of exception to L-4.2, where the Availability Percentage is less
| than 95.00%, the maximum aggregate Service Credit in respect of that Measurement
| Period is 50% of the Monthly Service Charge and the Service Credit is 50%.

L-4.3 does two distinct things and so is two exceptions at once: it displaces
the L-4.2 ceiling of 30%, and it displaces the L-4.1 percentage — in practice
band (d)'s 30% — with 50%. Neither alone would produce 50% of the Monthly
Service Charge: raising only the credit leaves the 30% cap biting, and raising
only the cap leaves the credit at 30%. It is therefore not folded into the
L-4.1 table, which continues to govern at and above 95.00%.

"Less than 95.00%" is strict, so exactly 95.00% stays in band (d) at 30% with
the 30% cap. The condition `availability_percentage < 95.00` entails L-4.1's
"less than 99.90%", so nothing further needs repeating from the parent.

```catala
scope ServiceCredit:
  label l4_3_cap exception l4_2 definition credit_cap_percentage
    under condition availability_percentage < 95.00
    consequence equals 50%

  label l4_3_credit exception l4_1 definition credit_percentage
    under condition availability_percentage < 95.00
    consequence equals 50%
```

## L-4.4 Arrears

| MSA-SCH4 L-4.4 (004-msa-sla-credits.md:82)
|
| By way of exception to L-4.1, no Service Credit is payable in respect of
| a Measurement Period in which the Customer is in arrears of any undisputed
| invoice for more than 30 days.

Two thresholds are strict. "More than 30 days" in arrears means 30 days is not
enough and 31 days is, and "undisputed" is the judgement input: an invoice the
Customer disputes does not engage the clause at all, whatever the arrears.

L-4.4 is expressed as an exception to L-4.1 but it forfeits the credit
outright — "no Service Credit is payable in respect of a Measurement Period" —
so it must also defeat L-4.3's 50%, and it therefore sits below `l4_3_credit`
in the chain. Its condition repeats L-4.1's operative condition,
`availability_percentage < 99.90`: a Catala exception does not inherit its
parent's condition, and without it this definition would apply in periods
where L-4.1 never engaged. Since a credit under L-4.3 also requires the
Availability Percentage to be below 99.90%, repeating that one condition
suffices to defeat both parents.

```catala
scope ServiceCredit:
  label l4_4 exception l4_3_credit definition credit_percentage
    under condition
      (availability_percentage < 99.90)
      and invoice_undisputed
      and (arrears_days > 30)
    consequence equals 0%
```
